  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN MULTI PARTNER TRUST FUND COLOMBIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The MPTF-C is a tripartite mechanism established by the Government of Colombia, the United Nations, and donor countries with the objective to support peace investments and efforts to implement the 2016 Peace Agreement between the Colombian Government and the FARC-EP. In 2019, the Fund entered its second phased with a focus in four strategic areas: Reincorporation, Transitional Justice, Victims, and Communications. Funding remains targeted at catalytic projects which complement Government funding to support the implementation of the Peace Agreement. During the second semester of 2022 the new Government requested the extension of the Fund and also to include a borader support to the Total Peace policy.</narrative>
  </description>
